The main text (before appendix.tex is input) ends on page 9. Looking at the structure of main.tex:

```
\input{analysis}
\input{conclusion}

\section*{Limitations}
...
\section*{Code and Data Availability}
...
\input{appendix}
```

The Limitations section and Code and Data Availability section are in main.tex itself. According to EMNLP rules: "Mandatory limitations and optional ethical considerations do not count towards this page limit." So Limitations doesn't count. But Code and Data Availability might count since it's not explicitly excluded.

The last page before appendix.tex is page 9, meaning the main text (including Limitations and Code/Data Availability which are in main.tex before \input{appendix}) spans pages 1-9.


Now I need to figure out whether pages 1-8 contain just the main content through the conclusion, with page 9 reserved for Limitations and Code Availability sections.
